  "description": "TEMVUF crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C101 H112 Cr1 Er6 N1 O40,2(C1 H4 O1),2(C3 H8 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er5 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er6 (Er) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.431-3.746 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.41-106.30°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CrEr6(OH)8(o-tol)12(NO3)(MeOH)5]·2MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Er(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
